2. **Color Patterns and Markings**: The coloration of needleleaf trees varies depending on the species. They generally have a mix of green needles and brownish-gray bark. Some species may also exhibit patches of lichen or moss, adding subtle variations to their appearance. The needles themselves can range from bright green to yellow-green, depending on the season and environmental factors.

